NAME
    cp - copy a file

SYNOPSIS
    cp SOURCE NAME

DESCRIPTION
    Copy the regular file SOURCE to a new file called NAME in the working
    directory. SOURCE may be a path; NAME is one name. The copy is a new
    file owned by you, whoever owned the original, and NAME must not exist
    already.

SEE ALSO
    mv(1), cat(1)
